steps.message:
The bug in `rich/segment.py` caused wide characters to be replaced by spaces when `Segment._split_cells` was called with a `cut` that fell in the middle of the character's cell width. I have modified the `_split_cells` method to split at the character boundary instead, ensuring that the original text is preserved. This means the resulting split may differ by one cell from the requested `cut` position when a wide character is encountered, but it avoids modifying the text content.

```python
# rich/segment.py

# Before:
            if cell_pos > cut:
                return (
                    _Segment(before[: pos - 1] + " ", style, control),
                    _Segment(" " + text[pos:], style, control),
                )

# After:
            if cell_pos > cut:
                return (
                    _Segment(before[: pos - 1], style, control),
                    _Segment(text[pos - 1 :], style, control),
                )
